rewrite notes -- where the work moved
=====================================
src/flash_kmeans.h      public C++ API (batch_kmeans, euclid_assign, centroid_update,
                        row_sq, kmeans_large_n[_assign])
src/kmeans_common.cuh   CUDA kernels: assign (shared tile / global fallback),
                        row_sq, normalize, rng_gather, accumulate (fp32 atomics),
                        finalize (mean, empty-cluster fallback, L2 renormalize,
                        max-shift tracking)
src/kmeans_launch.cuh   runtime launch configuration (device shared-memory limits)
src/kmeans_impl.cu      euclid/cosine/dot batch loop, convergence on max centroid
                        shift, deterministic splitmix64 random init
src/large_n.cu          CPU->GPU streaming: BLOCK_N chunks, double-buffered H2D,
                        cached ||x||^2, multi-GPU partition + gather-reduce-broadcast
src/bindings.cpp        nanobind module (raw pointers + current CUDA stream)
flash_kmeans/           thin marshalling only; same public API and module paths,
                        plus compat shims and a pure-torch fallback

Semantics preserved: fp32 accumulation, empty clusters keep the old centroid,
cosine/dot renormalize after every update, the returned centroids/labels follow
the original "labels from the last assignment" behaviour.
Performance at this commit (RTX 5090, fp16, B=32 N=74256 D=128 K=1000):
102 ms/iteration.
